   "body": "### The idea, in a paragraph\n\nEliminate serialization and buffer-copy overhead across the Go-to-Rust assembly trampoline (call_sysv.s / call_win64.s) by letting hy-check's existing loan checker (SPEC-LANGUAGE.md \u00a79) issue static stack-bound pin certificates for borrowed slices (&[]byte, &string). Currently, crossing into the Rust staticlib (serde_json, regex, sha3) requires copying payload bytes or marshaling across the bridge because Go's GC moving/stack-shrinking semantics forbid raw pointer retention across arbitrary calls. However, because Hybrid's assembly trampoline executes synchronously on a switched system stack with bounded two-tier budgets (Spike 1 & Spike 4) and cannot trigger a Go stack growth on the caller frame while suspended, any non-escaping loan proven exclusive by Tier-",
