   "body": "### The idea, in a paragraph\n\nIntroduce static task memory budgeting (task(budget = 16.MiB) worker()) certified by an allocation-effect contract at compile time. Currently, Hybrid proves data-race freedom across tasks (GUARANTEES.md Row 1) and memory safety via Go's GC (Row 17), but explicitly makes zero claims about memory exhaustion (OOM), task leak budgets, or allocation bounds. By coupling the escape analysis of hy-check with an affine capability-bounded allocation budget, every spawned task carries an allocation certificate verified against its static call graph. If a task cannot be bounded, it must either be marked unbounded (task(budget = unmetered)) or routed through an isolated arena/slab allocator that fails gracefully (or cancels the task scope) instead of killing the entire Go ",
