   "body": "### The idea, in a paragraph\n\nFor an opt-in certified subset, make neither `hy-check` nor `hy-emit` trusted for the emitted artifact's race-freedom claim. They produce Go plus a candidate permission derivation; an independent kernel checks that derivation against the **actual typed Go CFG**, including allocations, aliases, reads/writes and spawn/send transfers. A frontend ACCEPT or a certificate merely asserting \u2018sendable\u2019 is not evidence. The research question is whether explicit proof checking can remove inference/search from the trusted safety core without becoming another full checker.\n\n### Which assumption it breaks\n\nChallenge trusting `hy-check`'s implementation for the certified artifact's safety. At inspected main `1f0ff978f4deff78c77bca96db0e3e46f32de71b`, [stmt.rs:39\u201369](https://",
